# L §5.16: "A query that has no closed form is a statistic over paths: it stands only in an ask line that states
# paths N seed S (LOAD-ASKONLY elsewhere)"; "A query with where has no closed form". L §8.3 LOAD-ASKONLY `<query> has
# no closed form outside an ask`. (Writer 8: a closed-form query in a rule is computed, L5_16_query_closed_in_rule.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input g: dist
input lo: num
def mq: num = mean(g where g > lo) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  g = uniform(0, 1) to 0.01
  lo = 0.5 "s"

ask a: mq law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-ASKONLY mean(g where g > lo) has no closed form outside an ask ...
